From f52c3d49eec29ca5b26af6617a4587a1c28cc7ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:48:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] An online session in a room that is on has a link and a
 seat, and the room writes arrival and nothing else

Two migrations, each with its probe and its RLS section.

The first turns the lesson room on per department: edge_config.room_url,
lesson_platform_rooms, enable_lesson_platform (admin only; backfills the
link on future online sessions with none), a BEFORE INSERT trigger that
stamps new online bookings and never touches an UPDATE, room_access (host,
learner or observer, decided from the live booking inside its window),
manages_course, and the single-use lesson_tickets that room-ticket and
room-redeem spend.

The second gives a lesson its rooms, notebooks, consents, course-to-
materials mapping, transcripts, events and report drafts, and the RPCs the
room calls: lesson_room_state, my_online_lessons, lesson_join, lesson_end,
save_lesson_notebook, log_lesson_event, set_lesson_consent, and the
service-role door import_lesson_room_facts, whose probe asserts by regex
that it never names status, confirmed_start, requested_start,
assigned_teacher_id or meeting_url. retire_seed_course_twins is re-emitted
so the two new tables pointing at courses move with the rest.

The RLS suite passes on a fresh database (273 sections) and the ledger
says yes to all six new probes. RUNBOOK.md says how a room is switched on;
DEPLOYMENT.md gains the hourly ticket sweep in the pg_cron block.

