+## Turning the lesson platform on for a room
+
+The lesson room (room.mathvisionapp.com) is off everywhere until two things
+are set, and it is switched on one department at a time.
+
+1. Once per project, set the room's address:
+   `update public.edge_config set room_url = 'https://room.mathvisionapp.com' where id = 1;`
+   Null means off everywhere; a trailing slash is tolerated.
+2. Per department, as an admin, from the admin screen or the SQL editor:
+   `select public.enable_lesson_platform('<department id>', true);`
+   It records the room in `lesson_platform_rooms` and stamps
+   `meeting_url = room_url || '/lesson/' || id` on that department's FUTURE
+   online sessions that have no link yet — quietly: no push, nothing to the
+   portal. A Zoom link somebody pasted is never overwritten. New online
+   bookings in the department are stamped by the trigger
+   `session_requests_the_room_link` on INSERT only; a link a person clears is
+   never refilled.
+3. `select public.enable_lesson_platform('<department id>', false);` turns it
+   off: the row goes, every `meeting_url` stays as it is, and `room_access`
+   stops seating hosts and learners.
+4. Attendance for online lessons is written by the room — `lesson_join` as
+   the student, `import_lesson_room_facts` from the daily-webhook function —
+   onto `session_requests.arrived_at` / `departed_at` only. The booking's
+   status is never moved by the room: whatever closes online sessions today
+   keeps doing it, and a later portal sign-in still wins
+   (`import_portal_checkins` overwrites `arrived_at`).
+5. The hourly `mv-lesson-tickets` cron job (DEPLOYMENT.md, the pg_cron block)
+   deletes spent tickets; without it the table only grows, nothing breaks.
